    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The research plan lands on a disciplined Hold, and I concur. The structural bull case is real \u2014 golden cross (50 SMA above 200 SMA), $62.6B operating cash flow in six months, $61B in shareholder returns, and momentum across all timeframes with a breakout to all-time highs on elevated volume. However, the near-term tactical picture argues against chasing: RSI at 75.88 (peaked 79.58), price stretched 8.4% above the 20-day mean, ATR up 46%, and volume fading from 198M to 70M shares as price stalled and closed lower. With no fundamental catalyst confirmation available in this historical run, the risk/reward at ~$210.48 is asymmetric against new buying (4-14% downside to support vs 3.6-9.3% upside). The disciplined stance is to maintain existing positions, not add at current levels, and scale in on a pullback toward the $201-205 support zone with a hard stop below the 50 SMA at $181.51.\n\n**Entry Price**: 203.0\n\n**Stop Loss**: 181.51\n\n**Position Sizing**: Keep AAPL as a core holding at moderate weight; add 1/3 of intended position at ~$205 and 1/3 at ~$201 on pullback, reserving final 1/3.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
